CCA's source code and Python packages do not include the source code or binaries
of any third-party engine or model. It communicates with Stockfish (GPL-3.0) as a
separate UCI process and imports python-chess (GPL-3.0) and, optionally, Maia-2
(MIT). The web simulator includes third-party browser files (cm-chessboard, MIT;
chess.js, BSD-2-Clause; Cburnett chess pieces, BSD-3-Clause) with their licences
in cca/play/static/vendor/.

The container images published as ghcr.io/donquaan/cca are a combined
distribution: they also contain the Stockfish 19 binary (GPL-3.0-or-later) with
its licence, complete source and NNUE network in /usr/local/share/doc/stockfish/,
tini (MIT, licence in /usr/local/share/doc/tini/), python-chess (GPL-3.0-or-later)
and, in the -maia2 images, Maia-2 (MIT) and PyTorch (BSD-3-Clause); they never
contain the Maia-2 weights. The images are built on the python:3.12-slim base
image, whose Debian packages (including GPL and LGPL ones) and CPython (PSF
License 2.0) keep their own licences, as do the Python packages installed in
/opt/cca (licence files in their *.dist-info directories where the package ships
them). See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for what this means for redistributors.
